Subject: [PATCH] ppu_rules: build with -fcommon, as the GCC 7 era did

GCC 10 changed the default from -fcommon to -fno-common.  Homebrew written
against the old PSL1GHT toolchain (GCC 7) often defines variables in headers
without extern (`Sprite spritesheet;` in a header included by three files).
GCC 7 merged those tentative definitions; GCC 12 reports "multiple
definition of `spritesheet'" at the link.  AcidSampleV2 stops there.

ppu_rules is the Makefile path such code uses, so it gets -fcommon in
MACHDEP.  CMake projects (cmake/ps3-ppu-toolchain.cmake) keep GCC's default.

--- a/ppu_rules
+++ b/ppu_rules
@@ -18,7 +18,10 @@
 
 PREFIX			:=	ppu-
 
-MACHDEP			=	-mhard-float -fmodulo-sched -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections
+# -fcommon: GCC 10 and later default to -fno-common.  PSL1GHT-era code,
+# written for GCC 7, often defines variables in headers without extern;
+# those merged then and are "multiple definition" link errors now.
+MACHDEP			=	-mhard-float -fmodulo-sched -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -fcommon
 
 include $(PSL1GHT)/base_rules
 include $(PSL1GHT)/data_rules
